  "question": {
    "text": "Let the image of the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;in the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi><mo>:</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math>. let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#947;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;be a point that divides internally the line segment&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math> in the ratio <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>3</mn></math>. Then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>22</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#947;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "125",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Plotting the rough graph of the given data we have,</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/c4747631-1cec-4028-864b-038fabb26451-image.png\" style=\"width: 258px; height: 173px;\" /></p><p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math>&nbsp;be the mid-point of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8757;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mover><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#8869;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mn>11</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>M</mi><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>51</mn><mn>11</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>11</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>11</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Since&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;is mid-point of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi></math></p><p>So by using midpoint formula in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>M</mi></math>&nbsp;we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>62</mn><mn>22</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>23</mn><mn>22</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>40</mn><mn>22</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>, now comparing with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#947;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>We get,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>62</mn><mn>22</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>23</mn><mn>22</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>40</mn><mn>22</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>22</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#947;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>125</mn></math></p>",
